\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces KaryoFlow overview. (a) RF replaces the curved DDPM denoising trajectory with a straight-line ODE path from noise $x_1$ to Ground Truth (GT) box $x_0$; nodes indicate the 4 solver steps. (b) Time conditioning injects the continuous time $t$ via AdaLN-Zero zero-initialized modulation so the network is identity at $t{=}0$. (c) Coupling: Random pairing (orange) keeps full diversity $H(V \mid X_t){=}\log K$, while Sinkhorn-based Stochastic OT (pink) interpolates between hard OT and Random, with $0 < H(V \mid X_t) < \log K$.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method_overview}{{1}{3}{}{}{}}
