\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {XI}{\ignorespaces Annotation-noise robustness (Dataset~2 test, A3 checkpoint, seed~42, $1000$ images / $45{,}980$ GT instances). Rows: GT bbox jitter $\sigma _{\text  {bbox}}$ (px). Columns: GT class-flip rate $p$. Cells: \ensuremath  {\mathrm  {mAP}}{}@$[0.50{:}0.95]$. Clean baseline (top-left): $0.859$. The model degrades gracefully under mild noise ($\sigma {=}2$, $p{=}5\%$: $-0.193$ \ensuremath  {\mathrm  {mAP}}{}) and remains non-trivial even at the heaviest perturbation ($\sigma {=}10$, $p{=}20\%$: \ensuremath  {\mathrm  {mAP}}{}$=0.129$, still well above the $1/24{\approx }0.042$ chance level for class assignment).}}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:robust-noise}{{XI}{9}{}{}{}}
